Package: openmux-install-menu
Version: 1.4.0
Architecture: all
Maintainer: OpenMux <support@openmux.io>
Homepage: https://github.com/OpenMux
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: xz-utils, zstd, fdisk, rpi-eeprom
Description: OpenMux install medium boot menu (neutral utility)
 Plain-text install/rescue menu for the OpenMux USB install medium: install a
 target image to disk, a serial-number sub-menu for the console and for
 plug-in EX-12 adapters (program, identify and test, with the console's own
 FTDI chips held out of the way), a boot-order and bootloader sub-menu that
 shows the current BOOT_ORDER and both bootloader versions before writing (and
 refuses downgrades, frozen modules and unverifiable writes), run board tests,
 drop to a shell, reboot/power off, and toggle the stick's read-only root
 filesystem on and off.
 .
 The menu is a neutral utility only; autologin, the root shell profile, the
 read-only-by-default root (an overlayroot=tmpfs kernel parameter) and any
 other factory boot behaviour are not part of this package - they are applied
 by the openmux-install-medium layer at build time. Toggling means rewriting the
 single line of /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt, because the firmware appends that
 file to the kernel command line and ignores every line after it.
 .
 Every Depends backs a feature that degrades to a warning when its tool is
 absent: xz-utils/zstd decompress the embedded images, fdisk provides the
 sfdisk regenerate_disk_ids() needs, and rpi-eeprom provides the
 rpi-eeprom-config / rpi-eeprom-update the boot-order sub-menu reads and writes
 the module bootloader with. They are declared rather than assumed.
